  "_comment": "Shared golden fixture for the secret scrubber. Asserted by tests/test_secret_scrub_golden.py (Python) and brain-bar/Tests/BrainBarTests/SecretScrubberGoldenTests.swift (Swift) so the two implementations cannot drift. Every token here is synthetic: zeros or an alphabet walk. Any run of 16+ identical characters is written {{c*N}} and expanded by both harnesses before use, so no token-shaped literal is committed (GitHub push protection rightly blocks even all-zero ones). The file is ASCII-escaped so invisible characters (ZWJ, U+001C, combining marks) stay visible in review. Regenerate only together with a deliberate rule change in BOTH implementations.",
